   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Infrastructure</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Through the Advancing Multilateral Partnerships for Economic Development (AMPED) program, Australia partnered with the World Bank to provide technical assistance to the Philippine Department of Public Works and Highways (DPWH) to prepare and design the Mindanao Transport Connectivity Improvement Project (MTCIP). The MTCIP aims to improve connectivity, climate resilience, and the operational safety of roads in Mindanao. Australia&#x2019;s support for MTCIP included a review of the climate vulnerability of roads and recommendations to strengthen the environmental resilience of road networks in Mindanao. AMPED also helped DPWH meet environmental and social standards by preparing environmental safeguard instruments and documents. Australia&#x2019;s assistance was a critical element in the final design of MTCIP, and in March 2025 the World Bank approved a loan to the Philippine Government to improve infrastructure in Mindanao.</narrative>
    </description>
