    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Through the Australia-World Bank Growth and Prosperity Trust Fund Australia funded analysison how to hybridise over 200 diesel-powered mini grid systems at minimal cost. This advice was provided to the National Power Corporation (NPC), which owns and operates these mini grids. The results have implications for last-mile electrification as investments in hybrid mini grids have the potential to reduce the cost and improve the quality of energy services in remote and isolated islands.</narrative>
